=== 2026-10-29T10:58:28+10:00 worktree /tmp/mg-fix-davsync-read-cap on fix/wip-davsync-read-cap at 926ef769f ===
--- bug ---
A backup (or a usage file) read from WebDAV, S3 or GitHub with
io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(body, 64<<20)) is silently cut at 64 MiB. backup.Open
takes a body cut inside the sealed data for a damaged backup (ErrCorrupt), so a
sync's recovery treats an intact bigger file as damage: with this computer's
cached copy as the version that broke, it keeps the body as server-damaged and
writes the merged result over the file; where no cached copy matches,
described() still names the cut body a cut backup that Upload may replace.
--- fix ---
readCapped (internal/davsync/notbackup.go) reads maxRead+1 bytes and returns
errFileTooLarge when there is more: an error of its own, neither ErrCorrupt nor
ErrNotBackup, so sync, Restore and Upload return it and write nothing.
Call sites now use it: dav.go get, s3.go get, usage.go dav.read and s3.read,
and readAll (gzip/zstd/deflate results). unpacked's zlib try keeps that error
instead of falling back to raw flate. The 64 MiB cap is unchanged.
